## Entries and views

The server decides which **entry** opens a document (`Document.entry`): `form`, `view`, `report`, `list`, `page`, `web`, `auth`, `installer`. Each entry mounts its providers and a default layout, so an entity works with no client file at all.

A client file is an optional **view**: a React function with no props, named `client/<entity>-<kind>.jsx`, that adds behavior through hooks and paints the entry's layout.

```jsx
// client/task-form.jsx
import { useDocument } from "@loopar/document";
import { useForm, useFormEvents, FormLayout } from "@loopar/form";

export const config = { hasHistory: false };      // static flags of the entry

export default function TaskForm() {
  const { Document } = useDocument();
  const { getValue, setValue } = useForm();

  useFormEvents({ afterSave: (r) => loopar.notify(`Saved ${r.name}`) });

  return <FormLayout sidebar={<Notes />} />;
}
```

Only flags? `export const config = {...}; export { DefaultView as default } from "@loopar/document";`

| Import | Available in | Exports |
|--------|--------------|---------|
| `@loopar/document` | every entry | `useDocument`, `useViewOptions`, `useActions`, `useHandlers`, `useDocumentConfig`, `useFieldEvent`, `useFieldMeta`, `DefaultView`, `Layout` |
| `@loopar/form` | form, view, report, installer, auth | `useForm`, `useFormEvents`, `FormLayout`, `ReportLayout`, `BareLayout` |
| `@loopar/list` | list | `useList`, `ListLayout` |
| `@loopar/page` | page, web | `PageLayout`, `WebLayout` |

