## useDocument()

```jsx
const { ctrl, Document, name, entity, inModal, onClose, sidebarOpen, handleSetSidebarOpen } = useDocument();
```

| Property | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `Document` | Document payload (entity, data, structure, meta) |
| `name` / `entity` | Document name and entity name |
| `ctrl` | The controller instance (`docRef` is an alias) |
| `inModal` / `onClose` | When the document opened inside a modal |
| `sidebarOpen` / `handleSetSidebarOpen` | Sidebar state |

---

## useForm()

Form entries wrap react-hook-form. `useForm()` returns the form API bound to the controller:

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `getValue(field)` / `setValue(field, value)` | Read / write a field (marks the form dirty) |
| `getFormValues()` | Every writable field |
| `setError(field, { message })` | Show a field error |
| `save(options?)` | Submit through the document's action (insert/update) |
| `send({ action, document?, query?, extra? })` | Submit to any controller action |
| `validate()` · `hasChanges()` · `checkChanges()` | What `send` runs before the request |
| `form` | The react-hook-form instance |

```jsx
const { setValue, save } = useForm();
setValue("status", "Completed");
save();
```

---

## useFormEvents({ ... })

The client lifecycle of every `send()` — a `save()` or a custom action — in order:

```
validate()      built-in field validation → `validate` listeners → dialog + field errors, stops
checkChanges()  unless notRequireChanges                        → "No changes to save", stops
beforeSend      (values, ctrl, { action })  return false → stops
beforeSave      same, only from save()
── request ──
success:  form reset → afterSend → afterSave
error:    sendError → saveError → error dialog if nobody handled it
```

| Event | Signature | Return |
|-------|-----------|--------|
| `validate` | `(values, ctrl)` | `"msg"` · `{ field, message }` · array · nothing = ok |
| `beforeSend` / `beforeSave` | `(values, ctrl, { action })` | `false` cancels |
| `afterSend` / `afterSave` | `(response, ctrl, { action })` | — |
| `sendError` / `saveError` | `(error, ctrl, { action })` | — |

```jsx
useFormEvents({
  validate: ({ start, end }) => start > end && { field: "end", message: "End before start" },
  beforeSave: (values) => values.total > 0 || (loopar.notify("Empty order", "warning"), false),
  afterSave: (r) => loopar.navigate(`/desk/order/${r.name}/update`),
});
```

Listeners live while the view is mounted; inline objects are fine.

